<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85747" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορθμ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ferryman,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.187
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.158
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				633.104
			</span></i>(Milet., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1188.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.
			νεκύων,</span> of <i><span class="en">
				Charon
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				253
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				440
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>boatman, seaman,</i> esp. as one of the crew of a
			passenger-ship, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1086
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				1.57
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>conveyer, 'purveyor',</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν καθ᾽ ἡμέραν λεγομένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Or.</u>
					18.15
				</span></i>
			.</div>
